WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000 line:0%
And finally, new rule:

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.232 line:0%
Republicans have to stop
pretending they hate it

00:00:00.366 --> 00:00:03.369 line:0%
when celebrities give
their political opinions.

00:00:03.469 --> 00:00:06.239 line:0%
Please, you're the party
that made Reagan president!

00:00:06.839 --> 00:00:08.440 line:0%
(LAUGHTER AND APPLAUSE)

00:00:08.540 --> 00:00:09.476
It's...

00:00:11.744 --> 00:00:14.547
It's not our fault
that your celebrities

00:00:14.614 --> 00:00:17.850
are Ted Nugent,
Pat Sajak and Donald Trump.

00:00:17.917 --> 00:00:20.320
(LAUGHTER)

00:00:20.453 --> 00:00:24.457
James Woods? His last credit
was on a Mastercard bill.

00:00:24.791 --> 00:00:26.626
(AUDIENCE GASPING)

00:00:26.692 --> 00:00:31.364
(LAUGHTER AND APPLAUSE)

00:00:32.899 --> 00:00:35.769
Scott Baio? The only thing
he's been in recently

00:00:35.835 --> 00:00:38.104
that made headlines
was his co-star.

00:00:38.270 --> 00:00:42.042
(LAUGHTER AND APPLAUSE)

00:00:44.043 --> 00:00:46.779
Antonio Sabàto Jr.
was an underwear model

00:00:46.846 --> 00:00:50.016
who all the other
underwear models referred to
as "the dumb one."

00:00:50.116 --> 00:00:53.052
(LAUGHTER)

00:00:53.953 --> 00:00:56.989
And after he spoke at the last
republican convention,

00:00:57.156 --> 00:00:59.725 line:0%
he claimed he was blacklisted
in Hollywood.

00:01:00.259 --> 00:01:03.229 line:0%
Blacklisted?
Blacklist would be an upgrade.

00:01:03.295 --> 00:01:05.865 line:0%
(LAUGHTER AND APPLAUSE)

00:01:05.932 --> 00:01:10.370 line:0%
He wasn't on any list.
He'd be lucky to get on
a "Do not call" list.

00:01:10.436 --> 00:01:15.007 line:0%
(LAUGHTER AND APPLAUSE)

00:01:15.141 --> 00:01:17.510 line:0%
You'd have to run him
into show business.

00:01:17.743 --> 00:01:23.082 line:0%
(LAUGHTER)

00:01:23.316 --> 00:01:25.284 line:0%
And he's running
for congress now,

00:01:25.351 --> 00:01:28.221 line:0%
as is clueless
actress Stacey Dash...

00:01:29.055 --> 00:01:30.823 line:0%
who was also in the movie
<i> Clueless.</i>

00:01:31.023 --> 00:01:33.459 line:0%
(LAUGHTER)

00:01:33.559 --> 00:01:35.695 line:0%
At Obama's inaugural gala,
he had

00:01:35.795 --> 00:01:39.765
Beyoncé, Springsteen,
Sheryl Crow, Bon Jovi,
Mellencamp, Usher,

00:01:39.832 --> 00:01:43.636
Stevie Wonder, Garth Brooks,
Tom Hanks, Denzel and U2.

00:01:44.169 --> 00:01:47.073
Trump's inauguration...
had Jackie Evancho

00:01:48.440 --> 00:01:50.342
and the rock band
Three Doors Down.

00:01:50.409 --> 00:01:51.511
(LAUGHTER)

00:01:51.577 --> 00:01:53.546
As in,
three doors down from fame.

00:01:53.712 --> 00:01:58.151
(LAUGHTER AND APPLAUSE)

00:02:00.687 --> 00:02:05.991
And then there's Dana Loesch,
who America has come to know
as the fiery voice of the NRA,

00:02:06.225 --> 00:02:10.696
blaming gun violence
and all our problems
on Hollywood and its liberalism.

00:02:11.297 --> 00:02:14.400
They use their movie stars,
and singers, and comedy shows,

00:02:14.567 --> 00:02:18.271
and award shows to repeat
their narrative
over and over again.

00:02:18.338 --> 00:02:23.143
Fight this violence of lies
with the clenched fist of truth.

00:02:23.476 --> 00:02:26.179
(LAUGHTER)

00:02:26.245 --> 00:02:30.083
Yes, yes,
I know what you're thinking.
"Who hurt you, Danica Patrick?"

00:02:30.249 --> 00:02:35.288
(LAUGHTER AND APPLAUSE)

00:02:37.623 --> 00:02:39.391
What you may not... (LAUGHS)

00:02:39.491 --> 00:02:44.898
...know about Dana Loesch
is that before her job
as NRA spokesmodel,

00:02:45.365 --> 00:02:50.003
she was a show business wannabe,
a homemaker in St. Louis
with a mommy blog,

00:02:50.136 --> 00:02:52.972
and a radio show,
and dreams of TV stardom.

00:02:53.239 --> 00:02:58.978
<i>NCIS</i> producer Paul Guyot says
that ten years ago,
Dana pitched him a sitcom

00:02:59.245 --> 00:03:04.083
starring herself as, quote,
"a hot, young mom who does
a far-right radio show."

00:03:04.584 --> 00:03:06.386
Think<i> Frasier</i> meets awful.

00:03:06.552 --> 00:03:09.455
(LAUGHTER AND APPLAUSE)

00:03:10.456 --> 00:03:13.625
And you know what? If only
they had made that sitcom,

00:03:13.759 --> 00:03:17.063
today, she might be
a completely normal person.

00:03:17.196 --> 00:03:18.564
(LAUGHTER)

00:03:18.630 --> 00:03:21.600
Instead, we're all getting
the "clenched fist of truth,"

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:24.803
because show business gave her
the raised finger of "fuck off."

00:03:24.903 --> 00:03:29.709
(LAUGHTER AND APPLAUSE)

00:03:32.477 --> 00:03:36.915
The same thing happened to both
the founder of the right-wing
<i> Breitbart</i> website,

00:03:37.016 --> 00:03:40.686 line:0%
Andrew Breitbart,
who admits he came
to Hollywood "with the hope

00:03:40.753 --> 00:03:43.088 line:0%
that I'd eventually become
a comedy writer,"

00:03:43.756 --> 00:03:46.192
and to his successor there,
Steve Bannon,

00:03:46.492 --> 00:03:50.329
also a showbiz reject
who didn't have the talent
to cut it here,

00:03:50.395 --> 00:03:54.967
and so spent the rest
of his life hating Hollywood
and, by extension, all liberals.

00:03:55.401 --> 00:03:59.071
In his memoir, Breitbart
mentions Reagan six times,

00:03:59.272 --> 00:04:02.875
-and me 34 times.
-(LAUGHTER)

00:04:02.941 --> 00:04:04.777
True. He called celebrities

00:04:04.877 --> 00:04:09.248
"elitist pestilence,
with their cocktail parties
on the West Side."

00:04:09.314 --> 00:04:11.250
"God, I fucking hate them,"
he said.

00:04:11.417 --> 00:04:13.218
Which is funny,
because, you know, for years,

00:04:13.285 --> 00:04:16.522
you know who I'd always see
at cocktail parties
on the West Side?

00:04:16.622 --> 00:04:17.790
Andrew Breitbart.

00:04:17.856 --> 00:04:20.025
(LAUGHTER AND APPLAUSE)

00:04:20.092 --> 00:04:21.160
Oh, he...

00:04:23.296 --> 00:04:26.732
He hated Hollywood.
Hated it, hated it, hated it!

00:04:26.799 --> 00:04:29.569
Mostly from his home in
America's heartland, Brentwood.

00:04:29.802 --> 00:04:35.008
(LAUGHTER, APPLAUSE
AND CHEERING)

00:04:36.508 --> 00:04:40.179
As for Bannon, George Clooney
remembers him as, quote,

00:04:40.279 --> 00:04:42.882 line:0%
-"a schmuck who--" (LAUGHS)
-(LAUGHTER)

00:04:42.949 --> 00:04:46.351 line:0%
"...who literally tried
everything he could
to sell scripts."

00:04:46.585 --> 00:04:51.424 line:0%
Including, this is true,
a rap musical
of Shakespeare's<i> Coriolanus.</i>

00:04:51.824 --> 00:04:55.061 line:0%
Think<i> Hamilton,</i> but instead
of Founding Fathers, Romans,

00:04:55.128 --> 00:04:58.096 line:0%
and instead of
cultural phenomenon,
piece of shit.

00:04:58.263 --> 00:05:00.299 line:0%
(LAUGHTER)

00:05:00.566 --> 00:05:02.301
Bannon lost his shirt
on that deal,

00:05:02.402 --> 00:05:04.737
but luckily, he was wearing
three more. But--

00:05:04.803 --> 00:05:08.641
(LAUGHTER AND APPLAUSE)

00:05:10.643 --> 00:05:15.348
But trust me, if Bannon
could've sold a screenplay,
or Breitbart, a sitcom,

00:05:15.415 --> 00:05:17.783
they wouldn't have ended up
ranting and raving

00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:21.720
about cocktail parties
on the West Side.
They'd be attending them

00:05:21.920 --> 00:05:25.458
and, in Bannon's case,
finishing the drinks
people left on the table.

00:05:25.524 --> 00:05:29.662
(LAUGHTER AND APPLAUSE)

00:05:32.798 --> 00:05:37.669
-Including the ones with
a cigarette in them. And so--
-(LAUGHTER AND GROANING)

00:05:37.936 --> 00:05:41.607
That is why I implore, tonight,
all Hollywood execs:

00:05:41.673 --> 00:05:44.177
next time a conservative
comes to you

00:05:44.243 --> 00:05:49.681
with a really dumb idea
for a movie or a TV show,
just fucking do it.

00:05:49.781 --> 00:05:53.285
(LAUGHTER, APPLAUSE
AND CHEERING)

00:05:53.619 --> 00:05:55.688
We... (LAUGHS)

00:05:56.088 --> 00:06:00.092
We need affirmative action
for Republicans
in show business.

00:06:00.225 --> 00:06:02.528
They're not good enough
to make it on their own,

00:06:02.661 --> 00:06:04.897
but if we give them a leg up,
maybe they won't

00:06:04.964 --> 00:06:08.034
take their rejection out
on the whole country.
Huh, people?

